<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH BREWER RADEGAST Q1 GROSS PROFIT UP.</title>
<headline>CZECH BREWER RADEGAST Q1 GROSS PROFIT UP.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for three month period</p>
<p>ending March 31, 1997, according to Czech accounting standards</p>
<p>(in millions of crowns):</p>
<p> Gross profit		    97.71    vs	   59.76</p>
<p> Operating profit	     105.06    vs	   67.45</p>
<p>Sales of own goods</p>
<p> and services		   319.20    vs	  282.70</p>
<p> Output			   357.00    vs	  300.02</p>
<p> Total assets		 4,009.84    vs	2,772.78</p>
<p> Basic capital		  794.32    vs	  794.32</p>
<p>NOTE. Full company name is Pivovar Radegast a.s. .</p>
<p>The firm is the second largest brewer by market share in the</p>
<p>Czech Republic, which enjoys the highest per capita beer</p>
<p>consumption worldwide. Britain's Bass plc holds a 33</p>
<p>percent stake in Radegast. Radegast's shares are traded on the</p>
<p>main market of the Prague Stock Exchange (PSE). Results were</p>
<p>provided by the PSE.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
